1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,587
Please Lord, please.

2
00:00:09,016 --> 00:00:10,250
-Clean the cancer inside of her! -We need your help!

3
00:00:21,328 --> 00:00:22,453
What's it say?

4
00:00:23,038 --> 00:00:24,120
Miller Jones.

5
00:00:31,199 --> 00:00:32,620
-Get out. I told you last time. -Come on, now.

6
00:00:32,704 --> 00:00:35,120
Next time, the cops will drag you out.

7
00:00:35,204 --> 00:00:36,788
-Excuse me. -Get out!

8
00:00:39,346 --> 00:00:41,012
Did you need anything else?

9
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:42,780
Nah, I'm just passing through.

10
00:00:43,862 --> 00:00:45,321
On my way to West Virginia.

11
00:01:02,399 --> 00:01:03,487
I want you to finish it.

12
00:01:03,571 --> 00:01:04,780
You understand?

13
00:01:04,862 --> 00:01:05,946
Yes, sir.

14
00:01:13,355 --> 00:01:15,688
Hell, they having a little revival meetin'.

15
00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:22,337
-God!

16
00:01:22,421 --> 00:01:25,021
-Stubbs! -Stubbs, get out here, man!

17
00:01:25,438 --> 00:01:27,145
Now you remember what I told you?

18
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:47,037
Dad, no!

19
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,080
Dad!

20
00:01:54,746 --> 00:01:56,121
It's gonna be all right.

21
00:01:58,971 --> 00:02:00,887
Before I found the Holy Ghost...

22
00:02:00,927 --> 00:02:01,762
hiding under my mother's long skirts,

23
00:02:02,512 --> 00:02:04,512
spiders crawling through my dreams...

24
00:02:04,971 --> 00:02:06,430
Praise the Lord.

25
00:02:06,971 --> 00:02:09,512
The Lord looks out for me now!

26
00:02:13,377 --> 00:02:16,354
Helen did, in fact, meet the man she would marry that afternoon.

27
00:02:16,437 --> 00:02:18,062
Bless me, Reverend.

28
00:02:32,170 --> 00:02:33,588
I've heard your word.

29
00:02:47,512 --> 00:02:48,645
Mister, I do appreciate this.

30
00:02:53,769 --> 00:02:56,180
-Sister fucker. -He would do anything to protect her.

31
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:57,038
Though he wasn't one for praying

32
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:58,704
It was a sight you didn't end up in the hospital.

33
00:02:59,495 --> 00:03:02,095
Yeah, well, there's a lot of no good sons of bitches out there.

34
00:03:07,787 --> 00:03:09,138
-Happy birthday! -Oh, no.

35
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:18,303
Nice to meet you too. What you got there?

36
00:03:18,425 --> 00:03:19,508
and thirst...

37
00:03:21,255 --> 00:03:23,548
Preston loved the way people listened to him

38
00:03:25,010 --> 00:03:26,010
But friends...

39
00:03:27,199 --> 00:03:28,884
some of us are better off than others.

40
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:39,553
Reverend Sykes wept with me.

41
00:03:39,593 --> 00:03:40,675
To show yourself

42
00:03:49,743 --> 00:03:51,910
Do you really want these hands touching you?

43
00:03:58,927 --> 00:04:01,052
No, he's working, making deliveries.

44
00:04:01,176 --> 00:04:02,176
Is it Leroy?

45
00:04:04,133 --> 00:04:06,383
Don't act like you do nothing wrong.

46
00:04:12,742 --> 00:04:14,492
is you figure some way to get rid of it.

47
00:04:14,532 --> 00:04:16,707
living in that poor old woman's house who raised you.

48
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:19,805
No! No! No!

49
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,292
No, no, no!

50
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:43,779
lustful acts.

51
00:04:44,187 --> 00:04:45,771
Well, when you say anything,

52
00:04:51,485 --> 00:04:52,450
was just like this...

53
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:05,100
He was young, but that didn't mean she couldn't make it work.

54
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:06,712
Shit!

55
00:05:31,245 --> 00:05:32,004
Come on out so we can have us a talk!

56
00:05:37,699 --> 00:05:38,520
I had no choice!

57
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,930
I hate to be the one to tell you this, Sheriff, but your sister...

